# Definition of Ready

Do not start implementation (application code) unless DoR is met. See `docs/sdlc/definition-of-ready.md`.

Minimum for the DoR **gate** (SPECIFIED → READY), confirmed by a human:

- GitHub Issue exists
- Requirements in `docs/requirements/` without invented scope
- Functional specification in `docs/specifications/functional/`
- User stories and acceptance criteria in `docs/user-stories/`
- BDD in `docs/bdd/` derived from AC
- Test cases and a risk-based test plan exist
- Traceability rows exist (REQ → FR → US → AC → BDD → TC → TDE)
- Technical specification in `docs/specifications/technical/`
- Open questions marked `TBD — HUMAN DECISION REQUIRED`, not guessed
- Human has recorded Ready on the Issue

Unresolved business or technical questions that would force invented
decisions mean the item is **not Ready**.

Application implementation additionally requires a human-approved
**implementation plan** (READY → PLANNED). That plan is not part of
DoR. No `feature/` branch and no `src/` before `PLANNED`.

Docs-only or chore work may use a reduced DoR documented in the issue. Still do not invent product behavior.
